1. Scope

"Software" means this project's original code and documentation, and their
modified versions, accompanied by this license, to the extent the relevant
rights holders are entitled to license them. "Licensor" means a person entitled
to license the applicable material. This license applies only to versions or
copies accompanied by it.

Third-party software, libraries, fonts, images, documents, models, and material
identified as separately licensed remain subject to their own licenses and
notices. This license does not change those permissions, revoke rights validly
obtained under other earlier licenses, or limit non-excludable statutory rights.

2. Individual noncommercial grant

Subject to these terms, the Licensor grants natural persons a royalty-free,
nonexclusive, non-sublicensable license to download, copy, study, modify, build,
and run the Software solely for their own personal learning, experimentation,
or noncommercial academic research.

You may deploy the Software on a device or server you control, including a cloud
server, only for your own use. Access to the Software's functionality must be
restricted to you. Cloud hosting does not expand this permission.

Individual noncommercial use excludes use in performing duties or providing
deliverables for an employer, client, organization, or business, use for
commercial advantage or monetary compensation, and shared institutional, team,
or laboratory use. Ordinary personal learning and noncommercial academic
research are not excluded merely because the individual is a student or
researcher.

3. Uses not granted

Unless the relevant rights holders expressly authorize it separately in writing,
you may not:

a. Use the Software commercially, including for paid services or products,
   consulting deliverables, advertising revenue, API resale, or other activities
   for commercial advantage or monetary compensation.
b. Deploy or use the Software on behalf of a company, school, research
   institution, laboratory, team, or other organization, or provide an instance
   shared by its members, employees, clients, students, or other third parties.
c. Provide the Software's functionality to anyone other than yourself, including
   through a SaaS product, website, hosted instance, API, or deployment service,
   whether paid, free, sponsored, or supported by donations.
d. Sell, sublicense, relicense, or distribute the Software or modified versions
   to third parties, including rebranded, repackaged, or integrated versions,
   except for the repository collaboration permitted in section 4.
e. Remove or misrepresent copyright, license, or third-party notices, or claim
   that the Software is available under a different license.

4. Public repository and collaboration

The Software is source-available, not open source under the OSI definition.
Independent rights to view and fork under GitHub's Terms of Service are
unaffected.

Individuals may use the fork and pull-request features of public code-hosting
platforms for learning, modifications, and submitting fixes to the original
project in accordance with this license. Such copies and modifications must
retain this license and applicable third-party notices. This permission does
not authorize operating a service for others or republishing the project under
a different license.

5. Rights holders and separate authorization

The relevant rights holders reserve the right to use the Software commercially,
operate official paid services, release other versions, and grant separate
commercial or institutional licenses. A recipient of separate written
authorization may use the applicable material under that authorization. Public
repository access is not such authorization.

Requests for commercial or institutional permission may be made through the
maintainer contact channels listed in the project repository. No rights to the
project name, logos, trademarks, or official identity are granted.

This license governs copies of the Software; it does not replace the terms of
an official hosted service or automatically apply this license to users' own
input documents or ordinary generated translations or answers. Such content
remains subject to its own rights and applicable service terms.

6. Breach

The rights granted by this license terminate upon breach. Unless independently
authorized, you must stop the affected use, copying, modification, and
distribution. Reinstatement requires the relevant rights holders' written
consent. Third-party licenses and independent statutory rights are unaffected.

7. Disclaimer

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Software is provided
"AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE", without express or implied warranties, including
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or noninfringement. To that
same extent, the Licensor is not liable for loss arising from the Software or
its use, whether in contract, tort, or otherwise. Liability that cannot legally
be excluded or limited is not excluded or limited.
